-- title:
--   Generic fibre of the two-chart model of X₁(Mp): smooth, geometrically integral
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a nonzero natural number $M$ with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero which is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of order $p$, and let $\zeta \in L$ be a primitive $p$-th root of unity. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L = L((q))$, assumed equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), i.e. to the $L$-subfield of $L((q))$ generated by the image, under the coefficientwise map $L((q)) \supseteq \mathbb{Q}((q)) \to L((q))$ induced by $\mathbb{Q} \to L$, of the $q$-expansion function field [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionFieldC ℚ (Gamma1 (M * p))`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L134). Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with an $L$-algebra structure making $L$ its fraction field, such that $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ is in the image of $A \to L$, and let $K$ be an $A$-algebra compatibly with the tower $A \to L \to K$. Let $j \in K$ be nonzero and have image in $L((q))$ equal to the $q$-expansion $q^{-1} \cdot \mathrm{jNumQ}$ of the modular invariant. Then the base change along $A \to L$, that is the second pullback projection of [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.modelTo A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L252) against $\operatorname{Spec} L \to \operatorname{Spec} A$, is smooth of relative dimension $1$ and geometrically integral; here `modelTo` is the morphism to $\operatorname{Spec} A$ from the pushout of the two affine charts $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the subalgebras `chartAlg A K {j}` and `chartAlg A K {j⁻¹}` of $K$, induced by their $A$-algebra structure maps.
--
--   This records the two generic-fibre properties — smoothness of relative dimension one and geometric integrality over $L = \mathbb{Q}(\zeta_p)$ — of the two-chart integral model of $X_1(Mp)$ over a discrete valuation ring $A$ with fraction field $L$ and residue characteristic $p$. It is phrased in the hypothesis frame of the Abel–Jacobi and points statements for $X_1(Mp)$ over such an $A$, which cite it as input.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_XOneP_smoothOfRelativeDimension_one_and_geometricallyIntegral_baseChange_twoChartModel_x1_mul.lean

